## 6 EXHIBITION PLANNING


### 6.1  Operational Planning

For operational planning and control, the exhibition organizer shall:

- a) constitute dedicated teams with a designated team leader to execute and monitor the exhibition related activities;
- b) define and communicate the roles and responsibilities of each team member;
- c) provide training to the individual team member responsible for specific task;
- d) ensure the availability of necessary resources;
- e) sign an agreement with an external provider ensure effective and timely delivery of services;
- f) maintain ongoing communication with all stakeholders; and
- g) maintain documentation of operational planning activities and their implementation.
NOTE — For guidance, refer to Annex B for operational planning.


### 6.2  Exhibition Plan

The exhibition organizer shall prepare an exhibition plan in consultation with stakeholders, including



external providers. The plan shall cover all necessary procedures, arrangements, and resources required for organizing the exhibition effectively. The exhibition plan shall include, but not be limited to, the following aspects:

- a) Selection of the location and finalization of the venue in accordance with exhibition requirements;
- b) Prepare a detailed layout plan, including booth positioning, circulation areas, and service zones;
- c) Prepare a detailed day-to-day activity schedule, with allocation of roles and responsibilities for team members and external providers;
- d) Determination of space requirement (indoor, outdoor, covered or open areas);
- e) Identification of resources needed, including infrastructure, manpower, competency of key personnel, equipment and mechanisms for monitoring of external providers;
- f) Plan for visitor management, including circulation flow planning;
- g) Preparation of move in and move out plan for exhibitors, service providers and visitors with timelines;
- h) Planning of inauguration, ceremonies, and special activities;
- j) Preparation of a disaster management plan, including arrangements for medical assistance, where needed;
- j) Planning and implementation of VIP protocols, where needed;
- k) Establishment of a pre-registration process for visitors;
- m) Criteria and procedures for selecting and
engaging external provider;

- n) Preparation of a promotion and advertisement plan for the exhibition, including communication with exhibitors, and
- p) Preparation of a procedure for managing lost and found items, covering items received, record keeping and handling of unclaimed items.

