### 6.3  Exhibition Manual

The exhibition organizer shall prepare exhibition manual which shall include, but not be limited to, the following:

- a) Description and overview of the exhibition;
- b) A detailed execution plan and the duration of the exhibition;
- c) Constitution of teams, their roles, responsibilities and contact details;
- d) Site location, address and contact information;
- e) The venue layout;
- f) Participant guidelines (Do’s and Don’ts);
- g) Information on facilities and services available at the venue, such as restrooms, first aid, food and beverage;
- h) The details of engagement activities such as meetings, workshops, demonstrations, special events, opening ceremonies, and guest sessions;
- j) Safety and security arrangements; and
- k) Applicable legal requirements along with their compliance measures.

