### 6.4  Venue Finalization


6.4.1 The exhibition organizer shall conduct a detailed analysis prior to finalizing the venue, taking into account the type and mode of the exhibition (physical/hybrid). The venue analysis shall include, but not limited to, the following aspects:

- a) Location of the venue, its distance from the main city centre, and connectivity by road, rail, and air;
- b) Expected number of participants and adequacy of venue capacity;
- c) Availability of parking facilities;
- d) Logistics arrangements including transportation;
- e) Availability of accommodation in proximity to the venue;
- f) Prevailing weather conditions;
- g) Size and specifications of the venue, including hall dimensions, hall clear height, entrance/exit dimensions, hall flooring, load bearing or clamp load capacity, in-hall pillars, and other obstructions;
- j) Accessibility features, including ramps and wheelchair friendly routes;
- k) Emergency evacuation arrangements and exit provisions;
- m) Venue infrastructure, including electrical
wiring and fittings, air conditioning, compressed air, drinking water, cooking gas, and emergency lighting;




- n) Availability of an adequate number of toilets;
- p) Sufficient meeting rooms and spaces for meetings, workshops, demonstrations, special activities, opening ceremonies, guest sessions and the organizer’s office;
- q) Food and beverage facilities;
- r) Internet connectivity (Wi-Fi and leased lines options);
- s) Availability of nearby hospitals/clinics;
- t) Availability of PA system(s), CCTV, baggage scanners and other security equipment;
- u) Fire safety infrastructure and measures;
- v) Housekeeping arrangements including waste disposal facilities;
- w) Auxiliary areas such as registration zones,
lounges, and emergency room; and

- y) Availability of local support services (for example transport, fire station, police station).

6.4.2  In addition, the exhibition organizer should consider the following aspects at the time of venue finalization:

- a) Design the exhibition space to facilitate smooth movement of attendees;
- b) Ensure clear pathways, adequate circulation space, and multiple entry and exit points for visitors;
- c) Allocate suitable spaces for branding, signage, and promotional displays;
- d) Identify designated outdoor areas for assembly points; and
- e) Define conditions for cancellation or rescheduling of the exhibition.

6.4.3 The exhibition organizer shall obtain necessary insurance coverage to cover potential risks and third-party liabilities. All exhibitors and service providers shall also be informed to obtain their own insurance to cover the risks or liabilities during the exhibition.


6.4.4 In case the venue is not a registered facility (for example, private properties, open grounds, parks), the exhibition organizer shall obtain prior permission from local authorities before the finalization of the venue.

