- d) Control and monitoring mechanisms for the external provider’s performance to be applied by the exhibition organizer.

### 6.6  Safety and Emergency Planning

The exhibition organizer shall prepare and document a safety and emergency plan to ensure the safety and well-being of all stakeholders, including visitors, exhibitors, staff, and contractors, throughout the exhibition. The plan shall be developed, documented and made available to all concerned personnel. It shall outline preventive measures, roles and responsibilities, and emergency response procedures to manage and mitigate potential incidents



effectively. For guidance, refer to Annex C to prepare safety and emergency plan. The plan shall be reviewed periodically and updated.


### 6.7  Dismantling

The exhibition organizer shall ensure safe, systematic, and timely dismantling of the exhibition after its conclusion. A dismantling plan shall be prepared and communicated to all exhibitors, contractors, and service providers. The dismantling plan shall include, but not be limited to, the following:

- a) Define and implementation dismantling timelines;
- b) Scheduling of dismantling activities with minimizes disruption;
- c) Safety measures taken for the removal, transportation and storage of exhibits, furniture, carpets, signage, and temporary infrastructure;
- d) Assigning roles and responsibilities to team members and external providers for coordinated dismantling operations;
- e) Coordination with the exhibition organizer for waste disposal, recycling, and site cleaning; and
- f) Maintenance and retention of records of dismantling activities, including time taken, personnel involved, and any incidents or damages.
NOTE — The dismantling plan should consider environmental sustainability by promoting reuse, recycling, and proper disposal of materials wherever possible.

