### 7.2  Furniture

The exhibition organizer shall determine and document the quantity, type and placement of furniture required for the exhibition booths, lounges, meeting areas, and other locations. The furniture shall:

- a) be sturdy and suitable for its intended use and specified duration;
- b) be inspected prior to installation to ensure safety and stability;
- c) conform to relevant Indian standards, to the extent possible; and
- d) be installed and arranged by trained personnel as per agreed time schedule prior to exhibition opening.
NOTE — All furniture should be removed from the venue as per the agreed time schedule, after the completion of the exhibition.


### 7.3  Electrical

The exhibition organizer shall ensure an adequate and safe electrical supply to support all exhibition related activities. The exhibition organizer shall:

- a) identify and comply with all statutory and regulatory requirements related to electrical installations;
- b) ensure sufficient electrical load capacity to support the installation and operation of all installed electrical equipment such as air conditioners and heaters, including lighting installation, display screens, LED walls;
- c) engage the licensed electrical contractor for installation and testing of the electrical systems and equipment;




- d) execute a SLA with the external provider responsible for electrical support, covering performance, safety and maintenance requirements;
- e) ensure that all electrical equipment conforms to relevant Indian standards, where applicable;
- f) prevent exposure of live wires and ensure proper insulation and earthing throughout the venue;
- g) provide standby power backup systems such as generators, ensuring appropriate fuel safety, ventilation and accessibility arrangements;
- h) maintain load distribution to avoid overloading, tripping and fire hazards; and
- j) conduct regular inspection, testing and maintenance of the electrical installations and equipment to ensure functionality and safety.

