### 7.4 CCTV Surveillance

The exhibition organizer shall ensure the installation and effective operation of the CCTV system at appropriate locations for continuous surveillance and security. The exhibition organizer shall ensure the following:

- a) CCTV cameras are positioned strategically
to monitor entrances, exits, common areas, critical installations, and crowd movements;

- b) A dedicated control room is established for
real-time monitoring by trained personnel in coordination with venue security and local authorities;

- c) Video recordings of the exhibition shall be
maintained for the entire duration of the event and securely stored for a minimum period of seven days and a maximum of thirty days after the event;

- d) Only authorized personnel shall have
access to recordings, particularly in cases involving safety, theft, or legal incidents;

- e) Information boards are displayed at
prominent locations notifying attendees of CCTV surveillance to address privacy concerns;

- f) CCTV systems have adequate resolution,
night-vision capability, and uninterrupted power supply backup to ensure continuous operation; and

- g) Periodic inspection and functionality checks be conducted to ensure that all
