## 8 RELATED SERVICES AND FACILITIES


### 8.1  Facilities

The exhibition organizer shall ensure the availability of the following facilities including but not limited to, the following at the venue:

- a) Parking Facilities — The exhibition organizer shall establish, document and implement a plan for parking of vehicles during the exhibition for the stakeholders. The exhibition organizer shall:
- 1) provide sufficient parking to accommodate vehicles of stakeholders, including visitors, exhibitors, staff, logistics providers, and VIPs, based on the expected footfall;
- 2) include parking arrangements for freight forwarders, logistics operators, and service providers in the plan;
- 3) issue advance communication to stakeholders, regarding the availability of on-site and off-site parking facilities;
- 4) locate parking areas at an appropriate distance from the exhibition venue, ensuring safe and convenient pedestrian access;
- 5) create designated parking zones, as far as possible, for different categories of users, such as VIPs, exhibitors, service providers, logistics vehicles, and visitors; and
- 6) ensure that parking areas are located at a suitable distance from the exhibition venue and provide safe, accessible, and well-marked pedestrian pathways with clear signage, displaying parking availability, entry and exit routes.
NOTE — The exhibition organizer may engage an external agency to handle parking facilities as per the established plan.

- b) Washrooms — A sufficient number of clean and well maintained washrooms shall be provided preferably separate for males, females and individuals with special needs. The washrooms shall be cleaned at regular intervals as defined in the exhibition plan and records of cleaning activities shall be maintained;
- c) Drinking water — Safe and potable drinking water, certified by the concerned authority or conforming to relevant Indian Standard(s), shall be made available at appropriate location(s) of within the venue;
- d) Cloakroom — A supervised area shall be provided for visitors to securely deposit their personal belongings. An operating procedure for cloakroom operations and management shall be prepared and key instructions shall be displayed at the counter. The cloakroom shall be operational during exhibition hours under appropriate supervision;
- e) Lost and found counter — A designated counter shall be established to manage lost and found items. A documented protocol and incident reporting mechanism for lost and found items shall be established, implemented and integrated with the venue’s security operations. The records shall be maintained for all items received, as well as unclaimed items to be handled in




accordance with established procedures; and

- f) Seating and rest zones — Sufficient rest zones with adequate seating shall be provided at suitable locations for visitors, particularly for senior citizens, children, and persons with special needs.

